{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "From Past to Present", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Amish", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "religious", "type": "name"}, {"content": " faithful to or believing in a religion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Amish are part of a larger religious group of Anabaptist.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about the Amish.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "practice", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the repetition of an activity or skill", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Amman was believed to have started the practice of the community ignoring people after disobeying the rules of the church. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "wayward", "type": "name"}, {"content": "people who have lost their way spiritually or morally", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This was thought to have been the best way to remind the wayward of their sin while seeking to bring them back into fellowship.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a transgression or action that is against moral values or religion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Killing is a sin.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to seek", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Amish always seek a way to bring those that have strayed back into the church.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "plainly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without adornment or decoration", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They have continued to dress very plainly, using hooks instead of buttons on their clothes, while reflecting the dress of those who came before them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to shun", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to avoid", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Shunned people are expected to eat at separate tables at dinner time when dining with the others from the community.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Adverbial Clauses of Time, Reduced Forms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use adverbial clauses of time to show when something happens.  </br>Using adverbial clauses makes your speech and writing sound more dynamic and sophisticated.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Adverbial clauses of time are usually introduced by the time adverbs:  </br><span class=\"italic\">before, after, as, when, while, until, as soon as, since, no sooner than, as long as.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I like to read a book <span class=\"strong\">before I go to sleep</span>.</br> Will you wait here <span class=\"strong\">until I'm ready</span>?</br> I wasn't there <span class=\"strong\">when you came to see me</span>.</br><span class=\"strong\"> As soon as she got home</span>, she started making dinner.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Adverbial clauses of time can be placed before or after the main clause of the sentence. It is separated with a comma when it comes before the main clause, but the comma is not used when the adverb clause comes after the main clause.  </br></br>To make your writing more concise, you can use a <span class=\"underline\">reduced form</span> of an adverbial phrase. To do this, you need to make sure that the subject of both clauses is the same. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\"> I always take a shower <span class=\"strong\">before going to bed</span>. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They were shunned after disobeying the rules of the church. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It reminded the wayward of their sin while seeking to bring them back into fellowship.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In the 18th century, the Amish came to the US after being persecuted in Europe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They have continued to dress very plainly, while reflecting the dress of those who came before them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Shunned people are expected to eat at separate tables at dinnertime when dining with the others from the community. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Although times have changed, when being given the choice to stay or leave their communities, more than 85 percent decide to continue along their traditional path.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reporting Past Events in the Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In reports, stories and articles which refer to past events, it is common to use the passive voice. </br> You use a passive structure when you want the 'receiver' of the action to be the subject, rather than the 'doer' or agent.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the  <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past Passive</span> to report about finished actions or events that happened at a specified time in the past. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\"> It was Amman, who was believed to have started the practice of the community ignoring people.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past Passive</span> is: </br></br> subject + <span class=\"italic\">was/were</span> + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Passive</span> to report about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present. There is no specified time. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\"> Although they have been known to receive money or help from family members, they themselves are not allowed to give or do anything for the faithful. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Passive</span> is:</br></br>  subject + <span class=\"italic\">has/have</span> <span class=\"italic\">been</span> + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This was thought to have been the best way to remind the wayward of their sin.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many were thought to have traveled  to Pennsylvania to enjoy religious freedom.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They have been believed to have managed to keep their own special way of life by staying separate from the rest of American society.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The strictest Amish group has been known to have been the Old Order of Amish.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Although cars have been known to have been shunned by the Amish, they can accept a ride.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Amish have been renowned to have chosen not serve in the army, vote, or send their children to high school. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I watch the film <span class=\"italic\">Witness</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I note things that I find interesting about the Amish way of life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my opinions with a partner or group.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Watch the film <span class=\"italic\">Witness</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes of anything that you find interesting about the Amish way of life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your opinion of Amish life with a partner or group using the film as a base for your discussion.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn10le08ob07re2img03.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn10le08ob07re2img03.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "The Amish are part a larger religious group of Anabaptist. Their name comes from a Swiss Mennonite bishop named Jakob Amman. It was Amman, who was believed to have started the practice of the community ignoring people after disobeying the rules of the church. Shunned people are expected to eat at separate tables at dinner time when dining with others from the community.</br></br>Although they have been known to receive money or help from family members, they themselves are not allowed to give or do anything for the faithful. This was thought to have been the best way to remind the wayward of their sin while seeking to bring them back into fellowship."}, {"image": "engenn10le08ob07re2img02.jpg", "time": "39000", "id": 2, "text": "In the 18th century, the Amish came to the US after being persecuted in Europe. Many were thought to have traveled to Pennsylvania to enjoy religious freedom. They have been believed to have managed to keep their own special way of life by staying separate from the rest of American society.<br/><br/>The strictest Amish group has been known to have been the Old Order of Amish. They have continued to dress very plainly, using hooks instead of buttons on their clothes, while reflecting the dress of those who came before them. Although cars have been known to have been shunned by the Amish, they can accept a ride."}, {"image": "engenn10le08ob07re2img01.jpg", "time": "76000", "id": 3, "text": "The Amish have been renowned to have chosen not to serve in the army, vote, or send their children to high school. Although times have changed, when being given the choice to stay or leave their communities, more than 85 percent decide to continue along their traditional path. Their faith and taking care of each other holds them together."}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le08ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le08ob07re2img03.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about history and civilization.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about two connected actions. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about an unusual or unique event in life. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What do you know about the Amish people?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What other small religious groups are there in your country?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type":